# The demands filed as a range. One row per layer whose demand spans a width, so there is
# something a narrowing statement could actually reduce.
#
# The denominator for a receiver's one fact
#   This is the denominator for the one number a receiver is entitled to state as a fact. Judging
#   whether a narrowing sentence would narrow the range is prose and belongs to a person. Counting
#   how many ranges decline to say anything at all is arithmetic, and it turns "a claim without
#   one is weaker" from an opinion into a figure.
#
# The mirror of the point-value rule
#   It lives here: a range that files `narrowsWhen` as `notApplicable` is claiming it has no
#   range, in a row that demonstrably has one.
-- pm:Claim on pm:Demand where low <> high.
SELECT d.*
FROM (
    :compose(layers/demand.sqlc)
) d
WHERE NOT d.is_a_point
